# 8-Bit Calculator: RTL to GDSII Flow 🧮 

[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)

## 📌 Project Overview
This repository contains the complete **RTL to GDSII** flow for an **8-Bit Calculator**. Designed in **Verilog HDL**, this project implements fundamental arithmetic and logical operations and transitions them through standard digital physical design stages to generate the final GDSII layout. 

This project serves as an exploration into end-to-end ASIC design flows, bridging frontend logic design with backend physical design.

## ✨ Features
* **8-Bit Data Path:** Handles 8-bit operands for robust arithmetic and logical processing.
* **Operations Supported:**
  * Arithmetic: Addition, Subtraction, Multiplication.
  * Logical: AND, OR, XOR, NAND, NOR, NOT.
* **Status Flags:** Zero (Z), Carry (C), and Overflow (V) flag indications.
* **Complete Physical Design Flow:** Covers Synthesis, Floorplanning, Placement, CTS, Routing, and Sign-off.

## 🛠️ Tools & Technologies Used
* **Hardware Description Language:** Verilog HDL
* **Simulation & Verification:** ModelSim / Cadence
* **Synthesis:** Yosys / Cadence Genus
* **Physical Design (RTL2GDS):** OpenLane / Cadence Innovus 
* **PDK:** Skywater 130nm (Open-source)
* **Layout Viewer:** Magic / KLayout

## 📂 Repository Structure
```text
📦 8-Bit-Calculator-RTL-GDS-
 ┣ 📂 src/             # Verilog RTL source files (e.g., alu.v, calculator.v)
 ┣ 📂 tb/              # Testbench files for behavioral simulation
 ┣ 📂 synth/           # Synthesis scripts and netlists
 ┣ 📂 pd/              # Floorplan, Placement, CTS, and Routing reports
 ┣ 📂 runs/            # Run configurations and log files
 ┣ 📂 gds/             # Final GDSII layout files
 ┗ 📜 README.md